# Template for the per-environment env files.
#
# .env.dev / .env.test / .env.prod are TRACKED IN GIT and are the human-facing
# knobs for each environment. Kustomize reads them directly via
# configMapGenerator `envs:`, and scripts/render-env.sh checks them against the
# overlays.
#
# NEVER put secrets in these files. They are committed. Secrets go through
# Sealed Secrets — see docs/disaster-recovery.md.
#
# Copy this to .env only if you want to run the legacy docker-compose stack on a
# workstation (see README.md § Local editing). .env is gitignored.

# Home Assistant image tag. Pin an exact version — never `stable` or `latest`.
# A floating tag makes the deployment non-declarative: two syncs of the same git
# commit can produce different running software.
#
# This MUST match the `images:` newTag in the matching
# k8s/overlays/<env>/kustomization.yaml. `scripts/render-env.sh --check`
# enforces it, and CI fails the build on drift.
HA_VERSION=2026.7.4

# Host timezone. Must be a real tzdata zone name.
# `Etc/` only contains UTC, GMT and GMT±N — `Etc/Stockholm` is NOT a valid zone
# and glibc silently falls back to UTC, putting every timestamp and every
# time-based automation 1-2 h out. Use `Europe/Stockholm`.
TZ=Europe/Stockholm
